  Modifications by shoppilot:
    - common/settings.py
      Replaced with a slimmed configuration module that omits cloud storage,
      Elasticsearch, Redis, and database connector imports so that
      `from common import settings` does not pull in the full RAGFlow service
      stack. shoppilot only consumes RAGFlow's parsing and chunking layers
      (deepdoc.parser, rag.app.qa, rag.nlp.rag_tokenizer) and does not host the
      RAGFlow service.
    - common/token_utils.py
      Original code set `TIKTOKEN_CACHE_DIR` to the project root, which caused
      tiktoken to scatter 40-char hex-named BPE cache files in the working
      directory (polluting the repo). Changed to default to `~/.cache/tiktoken`
      (or honor an existing env var) so the cache lives in a conventional
      user-level location.

  Files in vendored directories that have NOT been modified retain the original
  Apache 2.0 license headers as authored by InfiniFlow.
